-- title:
--   Unfolding a pseudo-Eisenstein series against an automorphic function
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, with adele ring $\mathbb{A}$ and $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ carrying its Borel $\sigma$-algebra and Haar measure $\mu$, and let $d_1 < d_2$ be reals with $0 < d_1$. Let $\Phi \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ be contained in the determinant slab $\{g : \|\det g\| \in [d_1,d_2]\}$, where $\|\cdot\|$ is the idele norm given by the module of the distributive Haar character, and assume $\Phi$ is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ under `globalPoints` acting on $\mu$ restricted to that slab. Take the carrier pins `productionPinsOf` attached to $\Phi$, to the level-one subgroups, to the local Hecke generators and to the box `adelicBox` $\subseteq \mathbb{A}$; their central subgroup is all of $\mathbb{A}^\times$, their measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ is the Haar measure, their domain is $\Phi$, and their measure $\nu$ on $\mathbb{A}$ is the additive Haar measure conditioned on `adelicBox`. Let $\xi : \mathbb{A}^\times \to \mathbb{C}^\times$ be a character, let $f : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}) \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfy the automorphy predicate `IsAutomorphicFnAt` for these pins and $\xi$ (the `LsXiMember` condition for the Haar measure, the full central subgroup, $\xi$ and $\Phi$), and let $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}) \to \mathbb{C}$ be a slab profile for $\xi$: $\varphi$ is measurable, invariant under left multiplication by the unipotents $n(x)$ for $x \in \mathbb{A}$ and by the $F$-points of the lower-left-zero Borel subgroup, satisfies $\varphi(z g) = \xi(z)\varphi(g)$ for central scalars $z$, is bounded on every determinant slab with positive lower bound, and vanishes outside a band $a \le \mathrm{adelicHeight}(g) \le b$ with $a > 0$. Then $$\int_{\Phi} \Big(\varphi(g) + \sum_{\beta \in F} \varphi\big(w\,n(\beta)\,g\big)\Big)\,\overline{f(g)}\;d\mu(g) = \int_{\{q\,:\,\|\det \tilde q\| \in [d_1,d_2]\}} \varphi(\tilde q)\,\overline{\textstyle\int_{\mathbb{A}} f(n(x)\tilde q)\,d\nu(x)}\;d\bar\mu(q),$$ where $w$ is the adelic Weyl element, $q$ runs over the orbit quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ by the subgroup generated by the rational torus and the adelic unipotent group, $\tilde q$ is the chosen representative of $q$, and $\bar\mu$ is the quotient measure `rationalTorusUnipotentQuotientMeasure` built from $\mu$ and the Haar measure on that subgroup.
--
--   This is the unfolding identity expressing the pairing of a pseudo-Eisenstein (incomplete theta) series with an automorphic function as the pairing of the profile $\varphi$ with the constant term of $f$ along the unipotent radical, here in the truncated form in which all integrals are taken over a fixed determinant slab. It feeds the characterisation of functions orthogonal to all pseudo-Eisenstein series by almost-everywhere vanishing of their constant term, the approximation of slab profiles in $L^2$, and the residue computation for the Weyl intertwining operator.
